                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is weird. Really weird. But really fun, in all honesty. You drive these knockoff Fast And Furious ass cars through some pretty good tracks for money, get from place to place in a barebones open world, all while listening to some of the whitest music a person could listen to. Time trials are just you driving around in a circle to impress a girl you wanna sleep with. All of this is to say that the entire game is the embodiment of early 2000s car culture, endearingly so. It's like if NFS Underground had down syndrome. Also there's videos of the chicks in the game dancing to the previously mentioned white people music. It's... well, it's something.\n\nI will say though, you will need a couple fixes in order to run the Steam version. Mainly a widescreen patch because this doesn't go above 4:3 aspect ratios. Most widescreen fixes will mess up what little few controller fixes exist so personally I went with a Steam Translation Layer to sorta correct it (specifically Miro's. It's clunky but none of these fixes are perfect). Someone in the community hub also managed to get the uncompressed .mov files so if the compression bothers you, you have an easy fix. I would say to buy the GOG version but even that has a few issues just because of how weird the PC port is. Good game overall, though.",
